<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Nonsuch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1585</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Nonsuch was signed on 10 August 1585 at Nonsuch Palace in Surrey between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I of England</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rebels. Elizabeth agreed to send several thousand soldiers under the Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leicester">Leicester</a> and received the towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brielle">Brielle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Flushing</a> as security for her costs. The treaty brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> openly into the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> of 1588.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nonsuch.jpg" alt="Treaty of Nonsuch" width="320" height="564" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Queen Elizabeth I of England and the States General of the United Provinces of the Netherlands. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_of_Nonsuch.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
